{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SaGXfFkSCecbCcnXpD2CFQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The `inventory` service is fully implemented against the spec.\n\n## What I found and did\n\nThe service was already implemented through **v1** (in-memory) and **v2** (Postgres durability + row-locked no-oversell), but **v3 `ReturnStock` was missing across the entire stack** — only `server_v3_test.go` existed to pin the contract. I wired `ReturnStock` through every layer:\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `proto/v1/inventory.proto` | `ReturnStock` rpc + request/response messages (now matches all 5 spec RPCs exactly) |\n| `api/v1/*.pb.go` | Regenerated stubs via `protoc` |\n| `internal/store/store.go` | Added `ReturnStock` to the `Store` interface + `ErrExceedsSold` sentinel |\n| `internal/store/mem.go` | In-memory impl: NotFound if no record, `ErrExceedsSold` if `qty > sold`, else `sold -= qty` |\n| `internal/store/pg.go` | Postgres impl with `SELECT sold … FOR UPDATE` row lock for serialized read-check-write |\n| `internal/server/server.go` | `ReturnStock` handler (InvalidArgument on non-positive qty) + `ErrExceedsSold → FailedPrecondition` mapping |\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `go test ./...` — **all pass** (v1 + v3 in-memory tests green; v2 Postgres tests skip cleanly since `PG_DSN` is unset, as designed)\n- `go vet ./...` — clean; `go mod tidy` — clean, no stray `agentbench/*` requires (dependent_interface is empty)\n\nError codes match `error_semantics`: `InvalidArgument` (non-positive qty), `NotFound` (no stock record), `FailedPrecondition` (qty exceeds sold).\n\nI didn't touch any `*_test.go` files. Two things I **couldn't** verify in this sandbox, both environmental: `make build`/`make test` use the repo's `go.work`, which references sibling services (`booking`, `payment`, etc.) not present here — I built with `GOWORK=off` instead; and the Docker image build (daemon n